<description>
Extrapolate the moving sprite from a horizontal sequence of shared-border frames into the next standalone frame.

Input structure
- The grid is a row of equal-width framed panels sharing their vertical border columns.
- Each panel has the same fill color and one identical interior sprite at the same local columns.
- The sprite's top row changes by a constant amount from panel to panel.

Rule
- Build one output panel with the same height, frame color, fill color, and sprite.
- Continue the sprite's diagonal motion one more panel to the right.
- Because the output is a standalone panel, advance by the full panel width, not the shared-border spacing.

Key insight
- The panels are consecutive frames of motion; the output is the next frame after the sequence.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "identical interior sprite instances inside the shared-border framed panels",
  "path": "constant diagonal motion from panel to panel, continued one more standalone panel to the right; vertical offset is scaled from shared-border spacing to full panel width and rounded to the nearest row",
  "trajectory": "stamp one copy of the sprite in the next framed panel at the extrapolated row and the same local columns",
  "transform": "discard the previous panels; draw only the new single frame with the same frame and fill colors",
  "grid_shape": "same height, width of one standalone panel"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16 rows x 16-25 cols (always 16 rows in eval) [observed]
  panels:
    count: 3-4 equal-width framed panels sharing vertical border columns
    panel_width: 6-7 (interior 4-5 cols)
    interior_height: 14 (h - 2)
    frame_color: any ARC color; fills top/bottom rows and all separator columns
    fill_color: any ARC color != frame; most-common interior value
  sprite:
    shape: 1-2 rows x 2-3 cols bounding box, 2-5 colored pixels
    color: single non-fill color (may equal frame color)
    identity: same shape/pattern in every panel at same local column
    local_left_col: fixed across panels (always col 2 from panel left edge) [observed]
  motion:
    direction: vertical only (top_row changes by constant delta per panel)
    delta: integer in {-3..3}\{0}, constant across all consecutive panels
    all_positions_valid: sprite fits within interior [1, h-2] in every panel
  output:
    single standalone panel (same height and panel_width as input panels)
    sprite placed at extrapolated row = last_top + delta * panel_w / stride (rounded half-up)
    extrapolated position must fit within interior

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose height=16, interior_w in {4,5}, num_panels in {3,4}; panel_w = interior_w + 2
    2. Pick 3 colors (frame, fill, sprite_color); sprite_color may equal frame
    3. Design a small sprite (1-2 rows x 2-3 cols, 2-5 pixels of sprite_color, rest fill)
    4. Choose delta in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} and a starting top_row such that ALL panel positions
       AND the extrapolated output position fit within rows [1, h-2]
       Extrapolated top = last_top + delta * panel_w / (panel_w - 1), rounded half-up
    5. Build output panel: frame border, fill interior, sprite at extrapolated row
    6. Build input: concatenate num_panels panels sharing border columns, each with sprite
       at top_row + i*delta (i=0..n-1), same local column
